{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/980673-possess-living-rules-oversight-or-special-case","id":980673,"title":"Possess Living - Rules Oversight or special case?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-03T02:38:04-07:00","id":980673,"title":"Possess Living - Rules Oversight or special case?","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Living bodies require more than the Strix\u2019s power to keep healthy, and the Owls are often careless with their toys. The body will still starve to death if the Strix doesn\u2019t remember to eat and drink, and is still killed if all Health boxes are filled with lethal damage. If the body isn\u2019t completely destroyed (all Health boxes filled with aggravated damage) then the possession immediately changes to \u201cPossess Corpse\u201d as described above.&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an excerpt from the ability, and implies that death occurs at full lethal on the target. Furthermore, it suggests that this is the normal state of affairs, and that full agg = bodily destruction, not actual death.<br /> <br /> Except...that's not the case. Full lethal makes people bleed out, and they're dead when they hit full agg. Is this an exception for the power (doesn't seem like it, as the wording stresses maintaining the normal rules ('<b>still</b> killed'), or a rules oversight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T03:27:35-07:00","id":980686,"title":"","content":"I would classify that as a typo, although from a game mechanics standpoint, when your Health track hits full lethal, you start taking aggravated damage automatically unless there is medical intervention to stabilize the person and strix possession alone doesn't count as stabilizing the individual. Personally, I don't say a body is auto-destroyed when the health track is fully aggravated. For instance, you could be attacked and have your throat slit and enough damage done in that single attack to where you're unconscious with your Health track at full lethal and your attacker walks away. At that point it turns to aggravated as you bleed to death. Your bones aren't proceeding to snap like twigs and your extremities aren't falling off or crumbling to ash or whatever constitutes full bodily destruction..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:26:23-07:00","id":980816,"title":"","content":"The problem arises because a full track of aggravated means both complete organ failure and complete bodily destruction. You bleed out, you're at full agg and your body is intact. You get hit by a train, you're at full agg and you're body is in bits.<br /> <br /> Since Strix are usually NPCs the system just glosses over it, and says anything that hits one hard enough to wrap around to full aggravated probably destroyed the body, and anything less left it intact, and the host quietly died at some point leaving the strix piloting a corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:10:00-07:00","id":980855,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;still&quot; is a typo, and the mechanic is an exception to the normal death and dying rules to accommodate the transition from Possess Living to Possess Corpse. <br /> <br /> Normally, a character with full lethal damage is alive but unstable, upgrading wounds to aggravated until the health track is full of agg, and <i>then</i> they die. Corpses don't really need health, since they're already dead, and should probably be treated as objects, with Structure instead of Health. But, since animals don't have Durability traits, the rules just use the corpse's Health boxes and treat them like Structure, saying that they take bashing from everything and full aggravated damage means they are completely destroyed.<br /> <br /> Since it's extremely thematic for a Strix possessing a living host to kill the host due to carelessness and keep riding the corpse anyway, the Embodiment rules need to have a rule for transitioning from Possess Living to Possess Corpse. And since Possess Corpse says the body is completely destroyed at full agg, that can't be the point that marks the transition. So, Possess Living makes an exception to the normal death and dying rules, saying that the host simply dies at full lethal.<br /> <br /> It might be reasonable, if you want more internal consistency, to house rule that the host goes unstable as usual and dies when it reaches full aggravated, and then the health track is emptied and the Embodiment switches to Possess Corpse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}